## Phase ladder

Each phase has entry and exit criteria. Exit criteria are observable
(a test runs, a file exists, a tag is on origin) — not narrative.

### Phase 0 — Foundation (DONE)

- **Entry.** Nimbus on-prem still in service; tools still need to emit
  Visio for Nimbus import.
- **Exit.** Each sub-tool has a working pipeline + initial tests
  passing.
- **Status.** Closed 2026-04-24. All four sub-tools at 0.1.0; Nimbus
  path live via `.vsdx` emitter; ~570 tests passing across the
  workshop. Initial commits `76b4993` (compliance-matrix), `aac5728`
  (nimbus-skeleton), `cfc8ef7` series (process-tools-common).

### Phase 1 — Feature parity (MOSTLY DONE)

- **Entry.** Phase 0 exit; per-tool gap lists known
  (`requirements-extractor/REVIEW.md` was the canonical surface).
- **Exit.** REVIEW.md carryovers empty for the load-bearing tool
  (requirements-extractor); supporting tools have their initial
  feature surface complete and tested.
- **Status.** requirements-extractor 0.5.0 (2026-04-24) was the
  marker — REVIEW.md punch list closed, 469 tests. Subsequent
  additions extended the surface: 0.6.0 actor heuristics (the
  offline-network load-bearing fallback, +36 tests), 0.6.1 compound
  detection (+45 tests), 0.6.2 multi-action decomposition (+44
  tests). compliance-matrix added the fuzzy-id matcher (5th matcher,
  +20 tests). nimbus-skeleton added the review-writer enhancement
  (+3 tests). process-tools-common centralised `cli_helpers`
  (+9 tests) + `dde_xlsx` loader helpers (+8 tests).
- **Open against this phase.** requirements-extractor 0.6.1 and
  0.6.2 patch lines are uncommitted in the working tree (~7 days
  since authored 2026-04-27). Patch lines work — 559 + 44 + 45
  tests green — but the changelog Unreleased section will not
  cleanly close until they land in HEAD.

### Phase 2 — Camunda migration (IN PROGRESS)

- **Entry.** TIBCO Nimbus on-prem retired 2025-09-01; alternatives
  survey (`requirements-extractor/research/2026-04-25-stack-alternatives-survey.md`)
  confirmed BPMN 2.0 as the strategic interchange format.
- **Exit.** BPMN emitter output: (a) validates against Camunda
  Modeler 5.x desktop import — open and render with no errors and
  no warnings; (b) validates against demo.bpmn.io — same; (c)
  survives a Camunda-save-and-structural-diff round-trip with no
  semantic delta.
- **Status.**
  - BPMN 2.0 emitter shipped on `nimbus-skeleton` (Unreleased
    section) — 21 tests in `test_bpmn_emitter.py` covering
    structural round-trip, byte-stability, ID safety, BPMNDI
    section.
  - Programmatic structural validator 24/24 PASS
    (`research/2026-04-29-bpmn-structural-validation.md`).
  - Section-5 unittest pins 40/40 PASS in `nimbus-skeleton`.
  - **GUI gate OPEN.** Section-6 of
    `research/2026-04-29-camunda-import-checklist.md` (open in
    Camunda Modeler 5.x desktop, walk canvas, drop in
    demo.bpmn.io, save-and-diff) is the single biggest item
    gating v1.0.
  - Computer-use waiver landed in CLAUDE.md (Camunda Modeler 5.x
    desktop + Chrome MCP for demo.bpmn.io, scoped to QUEUE.md P1
    only). Waiver self-sunsets when the queue item closes.
  - **Operational blocker.** Scheduled Workers cannot service
    `request_access` interactive approval dialogs. Pending Eric's
    B1 (attended Worker session) / B2 (Eric runs the GUI step
    himself) / B3 (defer + drop `[in-progress]`) pick — open
    ~91h since worker-12pm 2026-04-30.

### Phase 3 — Hardening + commit hygiene (IN PROGRESS)

- **Entry.** Phase 1 closed; release artifacts depend on the working
  tree being a faithful image of HEAD.
- **Exit.** Zero uncommitted patch lines on `requirements-extractor`;
  zero ghost-diffs in `git status`; PyInstaller spec carries the two
  flagged hiddenimport gaps; CLAUDE.md role-file content drift
  resolved; orphan-dir tracking decision landed.
- **Status.**
  - **Open: 0.6.1 + 0.6.2 patch lines uncommitted** (~7 days). Two
    zero-risk P1 PROPOSED items would close: commit-or-stash
    (auditor 2026-04-29) + `git read-tree HEAD` to refresh
    `.git/index` (auditor 2026-04-30). Neither approved.
  - Open: `.git/index` ~118h stale; daily ghost-diff hazard.
    Workers commit via `GIT_INDEX_FILE=/tmp/...` plumbing-path
    workaround.
  - Open: PyInstaller spec gaps. Worker-10am 2026-04-30 audit
    flagged `yaml` (used in `config.py` + `keywords_loader.py`)
    missing from `_bundle()`, and `requirements_extractor.actor_heuristics`
    missing from explicit `hiddenimports`. Two-line spec patch
    proposed; not approved.
  - Open: edit-tool truncation hazard. Documented in CLAUDE.md;
    mitigation is bash binary-mode read+write. Surfaced again
    2026-04-29 on `models.py` (192 trailing NUL bytes stripped).
  - Open: role-file content drift. Three role files
    (`night-auditor`, `planner`, `worker`) exceed HEAD by
    +647 / +580 / +1938 bytes; mtime 2026-05-02 07:46 UTC.
    Eric's edit (active iteration); commit-with-intent
    recommended over restore-from-HEAD per worker-9am
    2026-05-04 analysis.

### Phase 4 — Bundle / cut / tag (NOT STARTED)

- **Entry.** Phase 2 exit (Camunda gate closed) AND Phase 3 exit
  (commit hygiene clean). v1.0-shape decision now locked
  (bundle, 2026-05-04) — no longer a Phase 4 entry blocker.
- **Exit.** Every sub-tool tagged at its final pre-1.0 version
  (e.g. requirements-extractor at 0.7.0, others at 0.2.0) with
  Unreleased sections promoted to dated entries; release-candidate
  bundle assembled; READMEs + CHANGELOGs current; PyInstaller
  bundles produced for the load-bearing subset (at minimum
  requirements-extractor; nimbus-skeleton if customer needs the
  emitters offline).
- **Status.** Not started. Depends on Phase 2 + Phase 3 close +
  orphan-dir tracked-vs-ignored decision. (v1.0-shape locked
  2026-05-04 — bundle.)

### Phase 5 — v1.0 release

- **Entry.** Phase 4 exit.
- **Exit.** 1.0 tags on each sub-tool pushed to `origin/main`;
  customer-deliverable bundle handed off; post-release
  retrospective in `DECISIONS.md`.
- **Status.** Not started. Expected scope: ~1 day of attended
  work once Phase 4 lands.

