## Current-state marker

Approximate weighted progress to v1.0: **~87%**.

Component breakdown (qualitative, not arithmetic):

- Phase 0 Foundation: complete.
- Phase 1 Feature parity: ~95% complete. Feature surface is in;
  the open delta is the uncommitted 0.6.1/0.6.2 patch lines, which
  is a Phase 3 commit-hygiene problem rather than a Phase 1
  feature gap.
- Phase 2 Camunda migration: ~75% complete. Emitter shipped;
  programmatic + unittest validators passing. The remaining 25%
  is the GUI gate, which is one attended worker session OR
  ~15 minutes of Eric's keyboard time.
- Phase 3 Hardening: ~65% complete. Code-quality green; commit-
  hygiene debts open. Two zero-risk P1 PROPOSED approvals would
  close the largest items.
- Phase 4 Bundle: 0%. Blocked on Phase 2 + Phase 3 + v1.0-shape
  decision.
- Phase 5 Release: 0%. Blocked on Phase 4.

**Single biggest open item: the Camunda Modeler GUI import gate.**
Closing it alone moves the toolkit from ~87% to roughly mid-90s,
because Phase 2 is 25% of the remaining weight and ~75% of Phase 2
is already done. Phases 3-5 are smaller and depend on Eric-side
approvals more than engineering work.

---

## Rate-limiter callout

The bottleneck on v1.0 is not automation throughput. It is Eric's
manual gates. As of 2026-05-04, Workers have hit 21 consecutive
empty-queue shifts on the rolling chain because every load-bearing
queue candidate needs Eric's explicit approval before it can be
picked up. The toolkit is feature-complete; it is waiting on
attended decisions, not engineering.

The four open Eric-side gates, in order of leverage:

1. **BPMN GUI option pick (B1 / B2 / B3).** Worker-12pm
   2026-04-30 NEEDS-INPUT. Closes the Camunda gate; advances
   Phase 2 to exit.
2. **Commit-or-stash 0.6.1/0.6.2 patch lines.** Auditor
   2026-04-29 PROPOSED P1. Closes the largest commit-hygiene
   debt; advances Phase 3.
3. **`git read-tree HEAD` to refresh `.git/index`.** Auditor
   2026-04-30 PROPOSED P1. Eliminates the daily ghost-diff
   hazard; restores morning-chain throughput.
4. **Orphan-dir tracked-vs-ignored decision.** Inputs in
   `DECISIONS-orphan-dirs.md`; the dirs are currently tracked
   but not formalized. Lands the cross-cutting cleanup;
   prerequisite for Phase 4.

Until at least one of (1) and one of (2)/(3) lands, the morning
worker chain stays empty-queue and Phase 2/3 do not advance.

